1
00:00:01,350 --> 00:00:07,170
And right now we can once again give a warm welcome to our mayor of New York City, Mayor Mamdani.

2
00:00:13,350 --> 00:00:14,786
My fellow New Yorkers.

3
00:00:17,542 --> 00:00:20,226
For 53 long years we have watched

4
00:00:20,614 --> 00:00:21,570
And we have waited.

5
00:00:23,014 --> 00:00:26,114
We have watched from nosebleeds and through gritted teeth.

6
00:00:26,502 --> 00:00:32,738
on televisions in the windows of electronic stores, and from projectors balanced on fire escapes.

7
00:00:33,542 --> 00:00:36,898
We have watched alone in our apartments with our heads in our hands.

8
00:00:37,542 --> 00:00:40,546
Shoulder to shoulder at bars where the signal flickers.

9
00:00:41,094 --> 00:00:47,554
alongside friends and family who we wish more than anything could be here today sharing this moment.

10
00:00:48,486 --> 00:00:52,258
For 53 long years, we have watched the Knicks and we have waited.

11
00:00:52,742 --> 00:01:02,498
We waited as the memory of Willis Reed winning the championship on one leg grew fainter and fainter. We waited as Clyde came up clutch again and again.

12
00:01:03,270 --> 00:01:07,842
as John Starks dunked on Jordan and Patrick Ewing dunked on the Pacers.

13
00:01:09,446 --> 00:01:12,034
as Bernard King scored 60.

14
00:01:13,286 --> 00:01:16,546
As Charles Oakley pulled every rebound within reach.

15
00:01:17,606 --> 00:01:20,002
As Spike got in Reggie Miller's face!

16
00:01:21,094 --> 00:01:25,474
as Allan Houston put up a shot against Miami that hung in the air for an eternity.

17
00:01:26,310 --> 00:01:30,370
as Larry Johnson gave us the four-point play heard around New York.

18
00:01:31,238 --> 00:01:36,290
as Starbury traded threes with Kobe and then sold sneakers every kid could afford.

19
00:01:36,678 --> 00:01:39,394
as Nate Robinson stuffed Yao Ming.

20
00:01:39,782 --> 00:01:42,818
As the city came alive watching Linsanity.

21
00:01:43,462 --> 00:01:48,130
and as Melo lived every Brooklyn dream when he came home.

22
00:01:48,550 --> 00:01:52,642
and made MSG feel like the center of the universe once again.

23
00:01:53,510 --> 00:02:01,602
We waited without ever knowing if this day would come and we waited because we knew deep down in our sick suffering hearts that it would.

24
00:02:02,566 --> 00:02:05,602
New York City, this team has done it.

25
00:02:05,958 --> 00:02:08,706
The New York Knicks are NBA champions.

26
00:02:13,222 --> 00:02:29,602
We are here not just because of this team that will go down in New York City legend. I'm talking about guys like Renaldo Balkman, Mardy Collins, Raymond Felton, Marcus Camby, Kristaps Porzingis, J.R. Smith, Iman Shumpert, and the whole Knickstape era.

27
00:02:29,990 --> 00:02:41,474
I'm talking about guys like Toney Douglas who I watched tie the single game franchise record for threes from the stands in 2011. I'm talking about Amar'e who got this whole city fired up when he joined.

28
00:02:42,630 --> 00:02:47,138
And I'm talking about Jared Jeffries and Lance Thomas and Langston Galloway.

29
00:02:47,462 --> 00:02:53,122
Players who gave everything, every game, even when a 20-win season was all that was in sight.

30
00:02:53,478 --> 00:02:59,138
This championship belongs to them too because championships aren't just built in one season.

31
00:02:59,462 --> 00:03:06,338
It belongs to Immanuel Quickley, R.J. Barrett, Donte DiVincenzo, Julius Randle.

32
00:03:07,750 --> 00:03:11,362
and also to a coach who helped lay the groundwork, Tom Thibodeau.

33
00:03:12,806 --> 00:03:28,994
Thanks to each of these New Yorkers and too many others to name, New York City has just had two of the most magical months in as long as any of us can remember. Over these past weeks, as the Knicks kept winning, our city has come together as one.

34
00:03:29,414 --> 00:03:40,002
Neighbors invited neighbors over. Strangers high-fived one another in the street. Subway conductors sang their announcements and bus drivers danced behind the wheel.

35
00:03:40,422 --> 00:03:46,946
So often when this city comes together, it is because we are forced to by a moment of tragedy or adversity.

36
00:03:47,270 --> 00:03:51,906
What a gift it is to be brought together by pure, unfiltered joy.

37
00:03:56,070 --> 00:04:07,042
For as long as we live, we will remember this feeling of a city together, a city alive, a city overcome by happiness. But let's not pretend that this was inevitable.

38
00:04:07,558 --> 00:04:10,754
If you will allow me, I want to travel back in time eight days.

39
00:04:11,142 --> 00:04:15,682
Game four, nine minutes and 33 seconds left in the fourth quarter.

40
00:04:16,358 --> 00:04:18,242
The Knicks are down 20.

41
00:04:18,566 --> 00:04:25,058
The analytics guys, the sports betting companies, the pundits who watch from far away, they do what they do.

42
00:04:25,382 --> 00:04:34,658
They run the numbers. They calculate the odds. They write the Knicks off. They give the Spurs a 99.6% chance of winning the game.

43
00:04:37,606 --> 00:04:52,130
A 99.6% chance of tying up the series 2-2, of reclaiming the momentum with the next game in San Antonio. A 99.6% chance of silencing the Garden, of another year of watching and waiting.

44
00:04:52,582 --> 00:05:01,538
But there is one thing that the pundits just don't get about this team. That they just don't get about this city. It is in that 0.4% that we go to work.

45
00:05:05,062 --> 00:05:10,882
It is in that .4% that Jalen Brunson, the same guy that so many said was too small.

46
00:05:12,326 --> 00:05:17,634
proves that not only is he good enough, he is the new standard for greatness.

47
00:05:20,326 --> 00:05:23,810
It is in that 0.4% that OG Anunoby

48
00:05:27,334 --> 00:05:39,330
Watch as the ball float from the top of the arc and start running toward the basket, fingers reaching towards the heavens. It is in that 0.4% that Karl-Anthony Towns

49
00:05:42,534 --> 00:05:55,522
Finds the strength to mourn his mother and still pull in rebound after rebound. Make block after block. It is in that .4% that Jose Alvarado shows every kid.

50
00:05:57,734 --> 00:06:05,506
growing up in public housing that a son of Brooklyn and Queens can win for every one of the five boroughs.

51
00:06:08,070 --> 00:06:14,018
It is in that .4% that Mitch breaks his finger before game one and says, "Go get the tape."

52
00:06:15,142 --> 00:06:17,378
It's in that .4%.

53
00:06:17,766 --> 00:06:25,794
That Josh Hart gets rebounds that break teams. That Mikal Bridges proves he was worth every single draft pick.

54
00:06:28,774 --> 00:06:32,002
that Landry Shamet pulls up from downtown.

55
00:06:34,374 --> 00:06:38,946
that every one of these 18 players transforms the franchise.

56
00:06:39,302 --> 00:06:42,242
that Mike Brown keeps this team believing.

57
00:06:46,214 --> 00:06:47,586
Most of all...

58
00:06:48,070 --> 00:06:58,210
It's in that 0.4% that the Knicks do what New Yorkers have always done when we are told something is impossible. We find a way. We win.

59
00:06:59,430 --> 00:07:03,266
Standing here before what feels like the entire city.

60
00:07:03,942 --> 00:07:07,106
There is a Jalen Brunson quote I can't stop thinking about.

61
00:07:10,502 --> 00:07:11,458
I'm gonna tell you

62
00:07:12,390 --> 00:07:15,810
You are allowed to think about the worst possible scenario.

63
00:07:16,198 --> 00:07:18,850
But you gotta go out there and do something about it.

64
00:07:22,246 --> 00:07:26,754
When Jalen Brunson took that pay cut, my friends, that was doing something about it.

65
00:07:28,870 --> 00:07:37,346
Time after time we thought about the worst possible scenario. And time after time the Knicks went out there and did something about it.

66
00:07:38,150 --> 00:07:43,426
The Knicks did not just win for New York City, they won like New York City.

67
00:07:44,550 --> 00:08:02,588
What is New York if not your back up against the wall? A dream that feels just out of reach? A rent payment you don't know how you'll ever make? What is New York if not 99.6% of the world stacked against you? And who are New Yorkers if not people who hear those odds and smile?

68
00:08:03,494 --> 00:08:08,450
who look at a 0.4% chance of success and ask, "Why are you giving me a head start?"

69
00:08:09,158 --> 00:08:19,330
This is our city. This is our team. For 53 years we watched. For 53 years we waited. Now we've won.

70
00:08:22,758 --> 00:08:26,946
One last time, New York, say it with me: Knicks in 5!

71
00:08:27,750 --> 00:08:30,018
Knicks in 5! Knicks in 5!

72
00:08:31,750 --> 00:08:32,930
Thank you so much.
